  "question": {
    "text": "A galvanometer has a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> and it allows maximum current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math>. It can be converted into voltmeter to measure upto <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> by connecting in series a resistor of resistance.",
    "image": null
  },
