  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>If we connect a high resistance(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>) in series with the galvanometer, it can be successfully converted into a voltmeter. Therefore,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/80e41353-0eed-4ef3-8e0e-fbba32ef01d0.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 83px;\"/></p><p>Voltage drop across voltmeter:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>19950</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
